  "researchNotes": "Official Armani Beauty sites (giorgioarmanibeauty-usa.com, armanibeauty.co.uk, armani-beauty.ca) returned HTTP 403 to WebFetch, so Armani/Prive names come from WebSearch results only. Fragrantica, Parfumo and most retailers also returned 403 or 404 to WebFetch, so their facts come from WebSearch snippets. Wikipedia pages were fetched directly and are used as publication sources. Concentration is conflicting for Iris Bleu (Harrods and Armani listings say Eau de Toilette; Perfumestars says Eau de Parfum) and for Acqua di Gio Profumo (retailers say EDP or Parfum), so those are left as recorded in the sources cited. Only a partial range was covered: Acqua di Gio and its Profumo flanker, Armani Code and Code Absolu, Si and Si Eau de Parfum Intense, and a set of Armani/Prive Les Eaux and Cuir Nu names. Other Armani/Prive collections and the main Armani lines were not covered. Armani Privé Rose d'Arabie was left out because its collection assignment could not be tied to a page that was read.",
